  abstract={Speech is the primary vocalized form of natural speech. Speaking is simple, hands-free, quick, and doesn’t require any technological expertise. Text is generated from spoken word sequences using automatic voice recognition (AVR). Having conversations with a computer Speaking is a more straightforward and pleasant method for humans to interact than using other devices like a keyboard and mouse, which need more hand-eye coordination and a certain level of competence. People with physical disabilities or those who are blind find using computers challenging. All of these problems are resolved by speech recognition. A speech recognition system has two main modes of operation: testing mode and training mode. When in training mode, the system listens to all of the speaker’s utterances and uses feature vectors to locate the matching utterances for each utterance.},
